; canary-A — SET 0 + LDB NULL (audit probe; W-START attempt-N5b)
; H_00:  SET state[0x50] = 0
;        LDB state[0x50] = zx(byte[mem[state[0x60]+0]])  (state[0x60]=0 → NULL)
;        RET
; Expected runtime outcome: the LDB tries to read from address 0
; (NULL). The Rust emulator's Mmu base is 0x1000; address 0 < 0x1000
; → read-OOB fault. Verifier behaviour: emits the same bytes; the
; *runtime* divergence is what we are observing. Per PROMPT-v3 §4S.3
; the lock-step behaviour is "host fault on bad addresses"; the
; emulator's ReadOob at NULL satisfies that contract.
; This is a FAIL-CLOSED canary, not a GREEN canary.
40 00
  30 50 00
  80 50 60 00
  FF
